<span class="enc-snip">The Archdiocese of Munich and Freising is a Catholic archdiocese in Bavaria, Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archdiocese-of-olomouc"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archdiocese-of-olomouc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archdiocese of Olomouc</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Archdiocese of Olomouc is a Catholic see in Moravia, in the Czech Republic, established as a bishopric in 1063 and raised to an archbishopric in 1777.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archdiocese-of-trento"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archdiocese-of-trento.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archdiocese of Trento</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Archdiocese of Trento is a Catholic see in northern Italy, traced back to the 4th century, when Saint Vigilius was among its early bishops.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archduke-ferdinand-karl-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archduke-ferdinand-karl-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archduke Ferdinand Karl of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archduke Ferdinand Karl (1754–1806) was a son of Maria Theresa and Emperor Francis I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archduke Franz Ferdinand was the nephew of Emperor Franz Joseph I and heir to the Austro-Hungarian throne from 1896.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archduke-john-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archduke-john-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archduke John of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archduke John of Austria was a Habsburg prince, son of Emperor Leopold II, who commanded Austrian armies against Napoleon and was a popular patron of Styria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archduke-rainer-joseph-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archduke-rainer-joseph-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archduke Rainer Joseph of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archduke Rainer Joseph was a son of Emperor Leopold II and brother of Francis I of Austria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archelaus-i-of-macedon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archelaus-i-of-macedon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archelaus I of Macedon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archelaus I was king of Macedon from about 413 to 399 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archelaus-of-cappadocia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archelaus-of-cappadocia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archelaus of Cappadocia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archelaus was the last king of Cappadocia, installed by Mark Antony in 36 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/archermus"><span class="enc-name">Archermus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archermus was a Greek sculptor of Chios active in the mid-sixth century BCE, from a family of sculptors that included his sons Bupalus and Athenis.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archery"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archery.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archery</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Archery is the use of bows to shoot arrows in hunting and warfare.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/archias-of-corinth"><span class="enc-name">Archias of Corinth</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archias was a nobleman of the Bacchiad family of Corinth who, according to Greek tradition, led the colonists who founded Syracuse in Sicily in 734 or 733 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archibald-v-arnold"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archibald-v-arnold.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archibald V. Arnold</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archibald V.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archidamus-iii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/archidamus-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archidamus III</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archidamus III was king of Sparta from about 360 to 338 BCE, son of Agesilaus II.</span></a></li></ul>
